From 949b91445809134ccb9b899093239a483a73cb33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 03:08:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/18] codec 32 (KLZH2): codec table, opt-in KOLMO_NATIVE=lz2,
 small-input coding, tests

codecs: C_KLZH2 = 32 with its table and memory row; KOLMO_NATIVE=lz2 maps zstd and Brotli to
it (lz and all keep codec 29, whose bytes do not change). No default writes it.
klzh2: short literal chunks may be tANS over bytes, short code chunks may use predefined
tables (fitted by benchmark/review40/klzh2/gen_pre.c), tables of about m/4 states.
tests: round trips at every level on inputs that reach each part of the format, every
truncation, bit flips and random bytes in headers and tables under ASan/UBSan.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FUEN4aRWhUw7yL7cZMqTmZ
