+     below 108. A literal length of 3 or more has a code in the literal-length stream: KLZH's length code of
+     (length - 3). Match length - 4 = v: v < 48 is code v, else h = floor(log2 v), code 48 + 2 (h - 5) + the bit
+     below the top, h - 1 extra bits (codes below 102); the code is in the first match-length stream when the
+     token's offset code is below 3, else in the second. A new offset of 16 or more (offset code >= 7) has, with
+     flag 1, its low four bits in the nibble stream and its h - 4 bits above them in the extra bits; otherwise its
+     h bits below the top are extra bits. The stream lengths follow from the tokens.
