+     reads; symbol i belongs to state i & 1. From 256 symbols: four states (symbol i: state i & 3) over two bit
+     streams: length of the first uv | the first (table header, four start states, the bits of the even symbols) |
+     the second (the bits of the odd symbols). All states must end at 0 and every stream must be consumed exactly.
+     Table header: L - 5 (3 bits) | last present symbol (7 bits; 8 for literals) | per symbol 0 .. last a 2-bit
